  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-10-17",
  "source": "Hager Electro / Herholdt Controls, \"Modbus Tables Summary\", rev. 1.14 (October 2022)",
  "sources": [{"title": "Modbus Tables Summary", "version": "rev. 1.14", "url": "https://assets.hager.com/step-content/P/HA_46515737/Document/std.lang.all/Modbus_table_Summary_V1_14.pdf", "note": "linked from the ECR380D and ECA380D product pages"}],
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers read with FC03; the writable ones use FC06.",
    "32-bit values are big-endian, high word first. Strings carry two characters per register, first character in the high byte.",
    "Values a model does not provide read as all ones (0xFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF, or 0x7FFF/0x7FFFFFFF for signed values). Single-phase meters have no L2/L3 values; the 1P 40 A meter has no partial energies.",
    "On CT-connected meters (ECx30xC) currents, powers and energies are primary values.",
    "The table gives no communication defaults; address, baud rate and parity are set on the meter and can be read at 0xC040-0xC041.",
    "Not in this map: the triple single-phase meters (ECx180T, ECx300T) energy tables, secondary-side values of CT meters, overflow details and the Read Device Identification and user block functions."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
